# AI EFFICIENCY RULES

1. Before editing, identify the smallest relevant set of files.
2. Do not scan or reanalyse the entire repository unless explicitly requested.
3. Implement one clearly defined task at a time.
4. Reuse existing architecture notes and implementation plans.
5. Avoid repeated searches and unnecessary tool calls.
6. Do not repeatedly run the full test suite; run targeted tests first.
7. Do not perform broad refactors or unrelated improvements without approval.
8. After two unsuccessful attempts at the same problem, stop, summarise the blocker and request direction.
9. Summarise changed files, tests and remaining issues concisely.
10. Ask for approval before starting any large-scale investigation or multi-stage implementation.
